WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.295
A 26-billion-parameter

00:00:02.107 --> 00:00:02.897
model on a

00:00:02.708 --> 00:00:04.477
24 gigabyte MacBook

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:04.772
Air

00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:06.064
Gall is a

00:00:05.876 --> 00:00:06.972
menu bar app

00:00:06.796 --> 00:00:07.798
that runs Thinking

00:00:07.610 --> 00:00:08.930
Machines' Inkling 2

00:00:08.742 --> 00:00:09.791
Mini on Apple

00:00:09.602 --> 00:00:10.604
silicon Macs

00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:12.220
with 24 gigabytes

00:00:12.032 --> 00:00:12.798
of memory

00:00:13.318 --> 00:00:14.155
The mixture of

00:00:13.990 --> 00:00:15.263
experts model has

00:00:15.075 --> 00:00:16.938
26 billion parameters

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:18.388
with 3.4 billion

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:19.320
active per token

00:00:19.509 --> 00:00:20.570
and Gall's own

00:00:20.382 --> 00:00:21.560
Rust and Metal

00:00:21.372 --> 00:00:22.716
engine generates about

00:00:22.528 --> 00:00:23.718
20 tokens per

00:00:23.530 --> 00:00:24.544
second on an

00:00:24.450 --> 00:00:25.829
M2 MacBook Air

00:00:26.366 --> 00:00:27.250
It unloads the

00:00:27.062 --> 00:00:28.205
model one second

00:00:28.017 --> 00:00:29.314
after each answer

00:00:29.243 --> 00:00:30.646
and saves conversation

00:00:30.458 --> 00:00:31.330
state to disk

00:00:31.390 --> 00:00:32.167
so your RAM

00:00:31.991 --> 00:00:32.946
is free between

00:00:32.758 --> 00:00:33.583
messages

00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:35.124
Full story on

00:00:34.935 --> 00:00:35.831
the dashboard
